<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Harness.Device</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Harness.Device</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    THE REAL IDeviceGateway. Everything else in src/harness is pure arithmetic; this is the one
    assembly that puts an object on a controller, and it does so by INVOKING THE EXISTING BINARIES
    rather than by re-implementing what they do.

    WHY SHELL OUT RATHER THAN REFERENCE. `openness-cli` and `download-probe` target net48 because
    Siemens.Engineering pins them there (docs/notes/openness-quirks.md); this assembly is net8.0 like
    the rest of the harness. A ProjectReference is therefore impossible in the direction that
    matters. It is also the direction we WANT impossible: TIA whitelists a caller by
    (Path, FileHash), so a harness that linked Openness would drag the whole approval cycle onto
    every harness build.

    THE ONE THING THAT IS LINKED is Ladder.Download (netstandard2.0, no Siemens reference, no
    network, no Portal). It is linked rather than reimplemented because the load manifest is the
    evidence the whole deployment verdict keys on, and a second parser for it would be a second
    opinion that could drift from the one the probe's own tests pin.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Loop\Harness.Loop.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Wire\Harness.Wire.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\download-feedback\DownloadFeedback\DownloadFeedback.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
